---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import TokenCalculator from '@/components/TokenCalculator.astro';
const site = 'https://www.ewohub.com';
const slug = 'stripchat-chaturbate-token-calculator';
---

<Base
  title="Stripchat &amp; Chaturbate Token Calculator: Tokens to USD"
  description="Free token calculator for models: convert Stripchat, Chaturbate, MyFreeCams and CamSoda tokens to USD, subtract studio share and taxes, and see what it takes to hit an income goal."
  lang="en"
  hreflang={[{ lang: 'en', url: `${site}/${slug}` }]}
  articleMeta={{ datePublished: '2026-09-24' }}
>

  <section class="art-hero">
    <div class="art-orb art-orb--1"></div>
    <div class="art-orb art-orb--2"></div>
    <div class="art-grid"></div>
    <div class="art-hero__inner container">
      <div class="art-meta">
        <span class="art-tag">Tool</span>
        <span class="art-tag art-tag--green">Free calculator</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="art-title">Stripchat &amp; Chaturbate <span class="art-grad">Token Calculator</span></h1>
      <p class="art-lead">
        Turn tokens into what you actually take home. Enter your tokens, your payout per token, your studio share
        and taxes, and see gross, net, and what you need to earn per hour to reach a monthly goal.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="art-body container">
    <div class="art-layout">
      <aside class="art-toc">
        <p class="art-toc__title">Contents</p>
        <ol class="art-toc__list">
          <li><a href="#calculator">Calculator</a></li>
          <li><a href="#how-it-works">How tokens become dollars</a></li>
          <li><a href="#gross-net">Gross vs net</a></li>
          <li><a href="#example">Worked example</a></li>
          <li><a href="#rates">Platform rates at a glance</a></li>
          <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
        </ol>
        <a href="#cta" class="art-toc__cta">Get help →</a>
      </aside>

      <main class="art-main">

        <p class="art-intro">
          Token math is simple until studio splits, payout tiers and taxes get involved. Use the calculator below
          with your own numbers rather than a generic average — every model's rate is a little different.
        </p>
        <p class="card-date" style="margin:0 0 1.75rem;">EWOhub Editorial Team · Published Sep 24, 2026</p>

        <section class="section" id="calculator">
          <h2>Token to USD Calculator</h2>
          <div style="margin-top:1.25rem;">
            <TokenCalculator />
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section" id="how-it-works">
          <h2>How Tokens Become Dollars</h2>
          <div class="glass-card" style="margin-top:1.25rem;">
            <p>
              Viewers buy tokens for real money and spend them in your room as tips, goals and private shows. The
              platform pays you a set amount per token, and keeps the difference between what the viewer paid and
              what you receive. That per-token amount is what the calculator uses.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
              Because viewers buy tokens in packages of different sizes, the platform's effective cut changes a little
              from purchase to purchase, but your payout per token stays fixed for your account or tier.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section" id="gross-net">
          <h2>Gross vs Net: What You Actually Keep</h2>
          <div class="reason-card" style="margin-top:1.25rem;">
            <div class="reason-num">01</div>
            <div class="reason-content">
              <h3>Platform payout (gross)</h3>
              <p>Tokens multiplied by your payout per token. This is the number platforms show in your earnings page.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="reason-card">
            <div class="reason-num">02</div>
            <div class="reason-content">
              <h3>Studio or agency share</h3>
              <p>If you work through a studio, you keep only part of the platform payout. Models commonly keep about 30–50% of what a studio receives, but the exact figure is in your contract. See <a href="/how-to-choose-a-webcam-studio">how to read a studio deal</a>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="reason-card">
            <div class="reason-num">03</div>
            <div class="reason-content">
              <h3>Taxes and payout fees</h3>
              <p>Withdrawal fees and income tax reduce what lands in your account. Tax rules depend on where you live, so put in a percentage that reflects your situation, or ask an accountant.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section" id="example">
          <h2>Worked Example</h2>
          <div class="glass-card" style="margin-top:1.25rem;">
            <p>
              Say you earn 10,000 tokens in a month at $0.05 per token. Platform payout is
              10,000 × $0.05 = <strong>$500</strong>. Working independently with 15% set aside for tax and fees, you
              keep <strong>$425</strong>. Working through a studio where you keep 40% and setting aside the same 15%,
              you keep <strong>$170</strong>.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
              The same tokens, very different take-home. That is why the split and the traffic a studio actually
              delivers matter more than the token count alone. More on realistic ranges in the
              <a href="/webcam-model-income-guide">income guide</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section" id="rates">
          <h2>Platform Rates at a Glance</h2>
          <div class="checklist">
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Chaturbate:</strong> flat $0.05 per token for standard accounts; Fan Club members can earn $0.06–$0.08.</li>
              <li><strong>Stripchat:</strong> roughly 50–60% of token value depending on status and traffic source; many models see a payout near $0.05 per token.</li>
              <li><strong>MyFreeCams:</strong> commonly cited as $0.05 per token to the model.</li>
              <li><strong>CamSoda:</strong> commonly cited between $0.05 and $0.055 per token depending on performance tier.</li>
              <li><strong>BongaCams and LiveJasmin:</strong> tiered percentages, so use your own current rate. See <a href="/webcam-earnings-by-platform">webcam earnings by platform</a>.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <p style="margin-top:1.25rem;">
            Rates change. Treat the presets as starting points and enter the rate shown in your own model dashboard.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="faq-section section" id="faq">
          <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-chevron" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>How much is a Stripchat token worth to a model?</span>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>It depends on your status and traffic source. Stripchat pays roughly 50–60% of token value, and many models see a payout near $0.05 per token. Your dashboard shows your actual rate, so enter that in the calculator.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-chevron" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>How much is a Chaturbate token worth?</span>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>Standard broadcasters get a flat $0.05 per token. Models with Fan Club status can earn $0.06–$0.08 per token, so switch the rate field if that applies to you.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-chevron" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>How many tokens do I need to earn $3,000 a month?</span>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>At $0.05 per token with no studio share and no tax, you need 60,000 tokens. Put your own share and tax into the target box in the calculator to see the number for your situation and how many tokens per hour it implies.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-chevron" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>Does the calculator include the platform's cut?</span>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7.5L10 12.5L15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>Yes, indirectly. The payout per token is already what the platform pays you after its cut, so use that figure rather than the price viewers pay.</p></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="cta" class="art-cta section">
          <div class="art-cta__orb"></div>
          <div class="art-cta__inner">
            <span class="art-cta__badge">Want more tokens per hour?</span>
            <h2>The calculator shows the goal. Traffic is how you reach it.</h2>
            <p>We help models bring viewers into their rooms so the token count actually grows. Tell us your platform and target.</p>
            <div class="art-cta__actions">
              <a href="https://t.me/+tBjfmjh9vHo1YzQy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="art-cta__btn art-cta__btn--primary">Talk to us →</a>
              <a href="/model-promotion" class="art-cta__btn art-cta__btn--ghost">Promotion services</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
          <h2>Related Articles</h2>
          <div class="related-grid">
            <a href="/webcam-earnings-by-platform" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">📊</span>
              <span>Webcam Earnings by Platform</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/webcam-model-income-guide" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">💰</span>
              <span>Webcam Model Income Guide</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/chaturbate-show-prices" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">🏷️</span>
              <span>Chaturbate Show Prices</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/stripchat-goals-tip-menu-structure" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">🎯</span>
              <span>Goals and Tip Menu Structure</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/best-cam-sites-for-models" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">🧭</span>
              <span>Best Cam Sites for Models</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/how-to-choose-a-webcam-studio" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">🏢</span>
              <span>How to Choose a Webcam Studio</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>

      </main>
    </div>
  </div>

</Base>
